# Documents, images and artifacts carrying real customer data — ANYWHERE in the tree.
#
# Two incidents shaped this rule. First: QA screenshots of the live app, saved to
# the repo root by a filename argument, escaped on 2026-08-17 (SEC-07, H-01) —
# `.playwright-mcp/` is ignored above but did not catch them. The earlier
# `qa-*.png` / `*.screenshot.png` pair only caught the two filenames that happened
# to leak; `calendar.png` or `trace.har` still walked straight past (@security L-08).
# Second: PO extraction work puts real customer purchase orders on disk — scans,
# photos and PDFs carrying customer names, addresses and pricing. Those live in
# subdirectories, so the root-anchored rules that fixed the first incident missed
# the whole class, and `pdf` was not covered at all.
#
# Hence repo-wide rather than root-anchored. Verified 2026-08-18: no image, PDF or
# binary file is tracked anywhere in this repo, so a repo-wide rule costs nothing.
#
# Real customer documents should live OUTSIDE the working tree entirely — an ignore
# rule you get wrong once is a history rewrite. This is defence in depth, not the
# plan. Committed eval fixtures must be redacted or synthetic.
#
# If a legitimate asset is ever needed (a logo under public/), add it with
# `git add -f` and note it here.
*.pdf
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.gif
*.tif
*.tiff
*.heic
*.har

# Root-anchored only. `csv` stays root-scoped deliberately — a seed or fixture
# dataset under db/ is plausible and legitimate, whereas `export.csv` at the root
# is the QA-artifact shape that leaked.
/*.csv
/*.log

# Prod values parked here while .env points at the local Supabase stack (docs/local-dev-setup.md)
.env.prod.reference

# Prod customer exports for local evaluations (Task 102). Real customer data, never committed.
docs/*.csv
